1. Quote ONE part of the ChatGPT that contains an ERROR;
- The 95% confidence interval of $51.60 to $60.09 for the mean price of textbooks means that the true average price of textbooks at the bookstore falls between $51.60 and $60.09.
2. Explain the mistake or flawed reasoning in the quote from ChatGPT's response;
- The mistake in this quote is that ChatGPT is implying that the true average price of textbooks definitely falls between this range, when in fact, with a 95% confidence interval, that only means we are 95% confident that the interval contains the true mean, not that we are sure of it.
3. Explain how to correct the error. 
- to correct this it would be better to state that "We are 95% confident that the population mean price of textbooks at a bookstore falls between $51.60 and $60.09"
